WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:05.350
Are you okay, Carmilla? Are you sick?

00:07.080 --> 00:10.610
Very humorous, suggesting that 
the greatest of the undead

00:10.610 --> 00:12.340
could get sick.

00:13.740 --> 00:15.870
Well, if you're sure.

00:15.870 --> 00:19.870
Someone might have me on their mind.

00:20.850 --> 00:22.990
You must be popular!

00:24.210 --> 00:26.080
You little flatterer!

00:26.380 --> 00:28.840
Your stew was quite flavorful, Lily.

00:30.070 --> 00:32.340
You're good at flattery yourself!

00:35.370 --> 00:37.410
Zenos! Welcome back.

00:53.070 --> 01:00.580
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

02:09.150 --> 02:10.440
I see.

02:10.440 --> 02:14.820
Undead being drawn to stronger undead, eh?

02:16.080 --> 02:17.380
You knew about that?

02:17.380 --> 02:19.950
I did not, but it's no surprise.

02:19.950 --> 02:24.580
I suppose my overwhelmingly charismatic 
aura must have also overflowed!

02:24.580 --> 02:27.960
Kneel down, human fools!

02:30.250 --> 02:33.050
What now? Will you kick me out?

02:33.050 --> 02:34.090
Nah.

02:34.380 --> 02:38.640
Given how you affect your surroundings, 
it's probably safer to keep you by my side.

02:40.010 --> 02:45.190
I... I want him to say that about me, too!

02:45.850 --> 02:49.630
"Lily. Stay by my side."

02:52.030 --> 02:54.210
Carmilla? Something wrong?

02:52.560 --> 02:56.440
It's 'cuz I'm Zenos's ideal wife!

02:54.720 --> 02:56.440
It's nothing.

02:57.000 --> 03:00.450
Asking a wraith, an entity despised 
by all, to stay by your side...

03:00.450 --> 03:03.200
You are as odd as they come.

03:04.140 --> 03:07.950
Very well. I will dedicate all my 
energy to being a nuisance, then.

03:07.950 --> 03:09.960
Did you actually think that sounded cool?

03:13.460 --> 03:18.450
Cresson, you seem to have performed quite 
wonderfully during the undead extermination.

03:18.450 --> 03:19.840
W-Well, sure!

03:20.090 --> 03:24.470
The other students who joined you 
have been singing your praises.

03:24.470 --> 03:26.100
It's impressive.

03:28.620 --> 03:31.620
That said, the fact that 
you did such an amazing job

03:31.620 --> 03:35.840
means that the special research student, 
Zeno, failed to live up to expectations.

03:36.620 --> 03:39.570
Continue to dedicate yourself 
to the professor's cause.

03:39.570 --> 03:42.000
You're free to go, Cresson.

03:42.000 --> 03:42.940
Right...

03:45.330 --> 03:46.580
Actually...

03:46.580 --> 03:48.360
I was awesome,

03:48.360 --> 03:52.330
but he—the special research student—
was actually really impressive.

03:52.330 --> 03:57.460
The hordes of undead and zombie king... 
He's the one who defeated them.

03:57.910 --> 04:00.210
What are you saying?

04:00.580 --> 04:04.140
The truth, sir. I saw it happen.

04:05.100 --> 04:07.030
If you'll excuse me.

04:10.930 --> 04:12.220
Damn it!

04:12.810 --> 04:16.250
We're even now, special research student.

04:18.270 --> 04:22.900
Zenos! The Goldran Research 
Lab is calling for you.

04:22.900 --> 04:24.780
Looks like you'll be invited to his faction.

04:24.780 --> 04:27.160
That's amazing!

04:25.020 --> 04:26.500
Really?

04:27.410 --> 04:29.760
I have to say, I'm impressed.

04:29.760 --> 04:32.960
I guess your undead extermination 
must've caught their eye.

04:32.960 --> 04:34.560
Huh...

04:34.560 --> 04:35.830
Are you surprised?

04:36.120 --> 04:40.710
I kinda thought the story was 
that Cresson took care of that.

04:40.710 --> 04:43.220
I'm not clear on the specifics, but...

04:43.620 --> 04:45.840
Guess this means we've cleared 
the first big obstacle.

04:45.840 --> 04:48.930
I'd think of it more as
reaching the starting line.

04:48.930 --> 04:51.720
You still have to be 
interviewed by the professor.

04:51.720 --> 04:54.450
What? There's still more?

04:54.450 --> 04:56.480
I was hoping this'd be more casual.

04:56.770 --> 04:59.180
Professor Goldran is a major mover

04:59.180 --> 05:02.300
who commands the majority of 
support in the Royal Hospital.

05:02.300 --> 05:04.820
He doesn't meet with just anyone.

05:04.820 --> 05:07.820
The more organized they are, 
the more of a pain they are, huh?

05:07.820 --> 05:09.830
I don't think I'm cut out for this stuff.

05:09.830 --> 05:14.200
And Professor Goldran is exceptionally 
particular when it comes to authority and honors.

05:14.200 --> 05:17.730
But isn't he an advanced healer?

05:17.730 --> 05:20.210
Doesn't that make you, an 
elite healer, more important?

05:20.560 --> 05:24.470
Unfortunately, political power 
and titles don't equate.

05:24.800 --> 05:29.090
Especially in my case, given that
I earned my title via developing drugs.

05:30.780 --> 05:34.100
Well, for now, I should probably 
go answer their call.

05:34.100 --> 05:36.020
I'll be praying for your success.

05:36.020 --> 05:38.380
You've got this, Zenos!

05:42.180 --> 05:43.940
Welcome, Zeno.

05:43.940 --> 05:47.070
I am the professor's second secretary.

05:47.370 --> 05:50.000
You're the special research student?

05:50.000 --> 05:52.330
What can you do?

05:52.330 --> 05:54.900
Healing's about the only thing I can do.

05:54.900 --> 05:56.960
How small...

05:56.960 --> 06:00.330
Any healer can do that.

06:00.330 --> 06:03.340
If you have power, then 
you should aim higher.

06:03.340 --> 06:08.460
You should know that healers hold 
special sway in our country.

06:08.460 --> 06:10.240
<i>Wait, they do?</i>

06:10.720 --> 06:14.010
You could even say this country's 
history is the history of healers...

06:14.010 --> 06:17.740
Yet, at the moment, the ruling class 
reaps the majority of the benefits.

06:17.740 --> 06:21.650
I intend to join them in the near future.

06:21.650 --> 06:25.340
This will ensure that our faction 
earns proportionate gains.

06:25.340 --> 06:29.150
Everyone deserves treatment equal 
to what they are capable of.

06:29.150 --> 06:31.030
That includes healers.

06:31.030 --> 06:33.880
Not all life is equal in value.

06:33.880 --> 06:35.950
It stands to reason that the wealthy

06:35.950 --> 06:39.040
and the impoverished would 
receive differing quality of care.

06:39.040 --> 06:43.790
Could you reproduce the magic circle 
you drew in your class right now?

06:43.790 --> 06:48.300
I'd like to see for myself whether 
or not you'll be of any use.

06:48.300 --> 06:50.430
And if you prove valuable,

06:50.430 --> 06:52.730
I'm prepared to welcome you.

07:01.500 --> 07:03.520
What exactly does this prove, though?

07:03.520 --> 07:06.750
The depth of your healing magic knowledge.

07:06.750 --> 07:09.900
And whether or not said knowledge 
has questionable roots.

07:13.410 --> 07:16.650
There are several different schools 
of magic circle conception,

07:16.650 --> 07:20.720
and with healing magic, there are certain 
principles that need to be minded.

07:20.720 --> 07:26.300
Any signs that they are not is an indicator 
that you did not receive an official education.

07:26.300 --> 07:32.360
Those who work for me must prove to 
be as legitimate as they are capable.

07:33.280 --> 07:35.270
What do you think, Professor?

07:35.800 --> 07:38.350
A fascinating magic circle.

07:38.350 --> 07:41.810
I've never seen these 
particular applications.

07:41.810 --> 07:46.020
And it does a fine job of minding 
the fundamentals, as well.

07:47.040 --> 07:49.060
You may join the lab starting tomorrow.

08:04.040 --> 08:05.000
What is all this?

08:06.020 --> 08:07.540
Look sharp, man!

08:07.540 --> 08:09.200
Hurry and line up!

08:10.220 --> 08:11.510
It's you...

08:11.510 --> 08:13.850
I'm Cresson, your senior in this group!

08:13.850 --> 08:17.180
Looks like you're a member of 
the Goldran Lab starting today.

08:17.180 --> 08:19.840
Which means you're gonna 
have to follow the rules!

08:19.840 --> 08:21.740
Sure, all right.

08:21.740 --> 08:27.470
I hope you realize the only reason you're a 
part of this is because I recommended you!

08:27.470 --> 08:29.150
You basically owe me your life!

08:29.150 --> 08:30.530
Really?

08:30.810 --> 08:33.650
Well, I am grateful. Why'd you do it, though?

08:35.030 --> 08:36.580
Isn't it obvious?

08:36.580 --> 08:40.040
I can use you to make my 
way up in the faction!

08:40.040 --> 08:42.090
You're an honest guy, huh?

08:42.770 --> 08:45.040
What's with the procession, anyway?

08:45.040 --> 08:47.750
It's for Professor Goldran's general rounds.

08:47.750 --> 08:50.460
He goes around visiting the patients

08:50.460 --> 08:54.170
with an entourage that he's at the head of.

08:54.170 --> 08:57.880
So... until I showed up, you 
were at the back of the line?

08:57.880 --> 08:59.420
Sh-Shut up!

08:59.420 --> 09:03.060
Just watch! I'm going to claw my way up!

09:03.060 --> 09:05.190
Okay. Good luck with that.

09:05.190 --> 09:08.220
Don't give me that pitying look!

09:12.010 --> 09:14.120
Does he really need all these people?

09:14.120 --> 09:16.270
It's all about creating an impression.

09:16.270 --> 09:19.410
Besides, the professor only visits 
people from the upper-upper crust.

09:21.290 --> 09:22.610
I wanna get a better look.

09:22.610 --> 09:24.790
Whoa! Where are you going?!

09:25.080 --> 09:27.290
<i>I need to know more about Goldran</i>

09:27.290 --> 09:29.920
<i>if I intend to find anything 
out about the disappearances.</i>

09:31.940 --> 09:37.300
Dr. Goldran, the pain has been so bad since 
I twisted my ankle on the side of the bed...

09:38.800 --> 09:41.050
It's a sprain.

09:41.050 --> 09:43.750
Three should be sufficient for this.

09:44.740 --> 09:45.630
<i>What is that?</i>

09:46.180 --> 09:49.270
Woven into a single ray of light,

09:49.270 --> 09:52.520
let the lost embers of life be your guidance,

09:52.520 --> 09:55.530
so that they may find their way home.

09:55.530 --> 09:57.360
Give Heal.

10:01.660 --> 10:03.660
The pain's gone!

10:03.660 --> 10:05.210
Thank you so much!

10:06.410 --> 10:09.080
Dude, don't just wander off!

10:10.630 --> 10:15.300
Sorry. But what was that magic 
where he used multiple healers?

10:15.300 --> 10:17.890
You don't even know that?

10:17.890 --> 10:20.970
The professor's specialty 
is health transfer magic.

10:20.970 --> 10:23.130
Health transfer magic?

10:23.130 --> 10:26.730
It's basically magic that transfers 
life force between people to heal.

10:26.730 --> 10:28.180
Pretty revolutionary, right?

10:28.180 --> 10:32.900
It can provide major results even if 
the caster isn't particularly powerful.

10:33.170 --> 10:35.760
Say you've got someone who's injured.

10:35.760 --> 10:38.880
You transfer someone else's 
life force into them

10:38.880 --> 10:42.110
in order to boost their recovery. 
That's health transfer magic.

10:42.110 --> 10:45.300
The worse the injury, the 
more life force it requires,

10:45.300 --> 10:47.360
so you need to prepare a larger number of

10:47.360 --> 10:50.890
healthy people to transfer the necessary 
bit of health to the patient.

10:50.890 --> 10:52.790
That way the patient is healed,

10:52.790 --> 10:55.810
and the burden on the donors is minimal.

10:55.810 --> 10:58.920
They only have to deal 
with a bit of exhaustion.

10:58.920 --> 11:01.000
That is interesting.

11:01.000 --> 11:04.150
It explains why he wants so 
many people for his faction.

11:04.150 --> 11:07.930
That's a part of it, yeah, but the biggest 
reason is probably the election for director.

11:07.930 --> 11:11.670
There are rumors that the current director, 
Shalbard, is going to retire soon.

11:11.670 --> 11:16.400
So he's trying to secure votes in 
preparation for the next election.

11:16.400 --> 11:19.650
At this rate, Professor Goldran's 
basically guaranteed to win.

11:20.980 --> 11:24.450
And if I ride the coattails of a winner, 
it'll mean a path straight to the top.

11:24.450 --> 11:26.800
I appreciate you filling me in like this.

11:26.800 --> 11:28.660
You're nicer than I figured.

11:28.660 --> 11:32.830
D-Don't be stupid! 
I'm just trying to use you!

11:32.830 --> 11:34.540
Since you're feeling so generous with info,

11:34.540 --> 11:36.720
I don't suppose you know 
someone named Afread, do you?

11:36.720 --> 11:38.420
Afread?

11:38.420 --> 11:43.180
The idiot who went missing despite the 
professor's hopes for him. Not a fan.

11:43.180 --> 11:45.180
Did anything seem off before he went missing?

11:45.180 --> 11:46.520
Hell if I know.

11:46.520 --> 11:50.290
He was invited to dinner and 
vanished right afterward.

11:50.290 --> 11:51.810
Dinner?

11:51.810 --> 11:55.910
The professor occasionally has dinner parties, and he invites all his favorites to them.

11:55.910 --> 11:59.030
Getting the invite basically guarantees 
you're one of his people in the future.

11:59.270 --> 12:01.880
Damn it! So jealous!

12:04.030 --> 12:06.890
This has all been very enlightening.

12:06.890 --> 12:09.460
Well, that about does it for me, right?

12:09.460 --> 12:11.540
Oh, hardly!

12:11.540 --> 12:15.670
This is a good hint, but still 
far from the evidence we need.

12:15.670 --> 12:19.640
The best thing to do would be to have you 
become one of Professor Goldran's favorites

12:19.640 --> 12:22.580
so that you could infiltrate 
one of these dinner parties.

12:22.580 --> 12:25.550
Pull that off and I'll pay you extra.

12:25.550 --> 12:27.090
In addition to making sure,

12:27.090 --> 12:30.550
as we originally agreed, that your 
underground operations aren't interrupted.

12:31.780 --> 12:34.560
I was kind of hoping to go home soon...

12:34.900 --> 12:36.970
However this plays out, once I'm done,

12:36.970 --> 12:39.150
I want you to tell me about my teacher.

12:39.150 --> 12:41.650
Of course. Everything I know.

12:46.060 --> 12:48.910
Zenos, I have a question for you.

12:48.910 --> 12:53.040
You see these coins scattered 
on the floor, yes?

12:53.040 --> 12:56.000
Now, I'd like to pick them up,

12:56.000 --> 12:58.860
but unfortunately, between 
research and meetings,

12:58.860 --> 13:00.920
I don't have the necessary time.

13:00.920 --> 13:04.420
So, if it was you, which 
would you pick up first?

13:06.350 --> 13:10.740
Do you believe that lives 
should be valued equally?

13:11.680 --> 13:13.930
Are you in, Dr. Becker?

13:13.930 --> 13:16.940
Oh, Zenos is here, too.

13:16.940 --> 13:18.740
Am I interrupting?

13:18.740 --> 13:21.750
Not at all. Just chatting a bit.

13:21.750 --> 13:23.310
I've got a meeting, right?

13:23.310 --> 13:24.900
Where was it again?

13:24.900 --> 13:27.920
Ugh... I'll show you the way.

13:27.920 --> 13:30.030
I'm always in your debt.

13:30.560 --> 13:32.290
I'm counting on you.

13:36.040 --> 13:38.320
I'll do what I can.

13:47.690 --> 13:50.110
Lynga might be a genius!

13:52.300 --> 13:57.600
Now I can sneak into Sir Zenos's bed on 
my own and sniff it as much as I want!

13:59.980 --> 14:01.360
Zophia?!

13:59.980 --> 14:01.360
Lynga?!

14:01.360 --> 14:03.110
What are you doing here?!

14:03.110 --> 14:04.990
I was gonna ask you the same thing.

14:06.480 --> 14:07.780
Oh, I see.

14:07.780 --> 14:09.700
You came to clean up, too?

14:09.700 --> 14:11.040
You, too?

14:12.280 --> 14:17.540
I'm a genius! Who else would think of 
cleaning the clinic while Zenos was out?!

14:18.770 --> 14:21.640
I kinda saw this coming, y'know.

14:21.640 --> 14:25.130
And a broken door means even more work...

14:25.940 --> 14:28.810
I guess the two of you showed up ahead of me.

14:39.840 --> 14:42.770
This is looking good! I did a fine job!

14:42.770 --> 14:45.280
Lynga did over half the work!

14:45.280 --> 14:47.860
And I have perfectly repaired the door!

14:47.860 --> 14:50.120
You're the one who broke it!

14:58.260 --> 15:02.420
I'm providing you the opportunity 
to help my glorious self!

15:02.420 --> 15:04.610
That means looking after the 
professor's beloved pup!

15:05.750 --> 15:08.090
You just have to watch her.

15:09.020 --> 15:13.920
Uh... you do more stuff for 
the lab than this, right?

15:13.920 --> 15:15.390
Of course I do!

15:15.390 --> 15:18.520
Other than walks, I also provide 
Madam Milk with her meals!

15:18.520 --> 15:22.280
In addition to washing 
and grooming... and more!

15:22.280 --> 15:24.520
Not exactly the answer I was expecting.

15:24.520 --> 15:29.400
The professor's meeting with the seven 
major nobles that he's currying favor with.

15:29.400 --> 15:31.740
Man, that's so cool!

15:31.740 --> 15:34.900
Then again, if I climb my way 
up the faction's ladder,

15:34.900 --> 15:38.430
I could be in the same position soon enough!

15:38.430 --> 15:40.540
You're hoping for a promotion, then?

15:41.130 --> 15:42.640
Of course I am!

15:42.640 --> 15:45.420
Once I become a big deal 
and join the upper crust,

15:45.420 --> 15:50.010
I'll have good food, good women, 
and peons to push around!

15:50.010 --> 15:52.880
That's why I'm working hard to be a healer!

15:53.200 --> 15:57.010
I thought being a healer was 
about, y'know, healing people.

15:57.840 --> 15:59.750
Ideally, maybe.

15:59.750 --> 16:01.790
I mean, sure, even I had a time when

16:01.790 --> 16:05.930
I dreamed about saving a bunch of 
lives or curing a terrible disease,

16:05.930 --> 16:08.480
but healing magic isn't all-powerful.

16:08.480 --> 16:10.490
There are things it just can't do.

16:10.490 --> 16:13.360
Y'know what's more reliable? Money and power!

16:15.120 --> 16:16.270
What?

16:16.270 --> 16:18.120
Hey, Cresson!

16:18.430 --> 16:21.790
Looking after Goldran's 
high and mighty mutt again?

16:21.790 --> 16:23.250
Mr. Bons!

16:23.250 --> 16:25.250
I'm doing what I can, yes.

16:25.650 --> 16:27.250
Damn it all...

16:27.250 --> 16:30.210
That is one smug-looking mutt.

16:30.490 --> 16:31.840
Ticks me off.

16:31.840 --> 16:34.750
Don't let the professor 
hear you say that, sir!

16:35.360 --> 16:37.810
Takes more than sucking up 
to get anywhere in life, boy.

16:39.260 --> 16:40.370
Who was that?

16:40.370 --> 16:42.850
Professor Goldran's first secretary.

16:43.150 --> 16:44.130
That guy?

16:44.130 --> 16:45.820
Unbelievable, right?

16:45.820 --> 16:49.140
They're apparently old friends, 
but he barely does any work,

16:49.140 --> 16:51.740
and he's usually drunk all day long.

16:51.740 --> 16:57.490
Can't believe he gets the spot of first 
secretary, even if they do go way back.

16:57.490 --> 16:58.760
Hey, Cresson!

16:58.760 --> 17:01.120
Y-Yes?! You called for me?

17:01.120 --> 17:03.000
You can have this booze!

17:06.640 --> 17:08.800
Oh, no! Madam Milk!

17:14.220 --> 17:16.340
Milk! Milk!

17:30.040 --> 17:32.110
Light of life that dwells deep within,

17:32.110 --> 17:35.610
hear my prayers, and let your 
blessing shine forth here!

17:35.610 --> 17:36.930
High Heal!

17:38.530 --> 17:40.520
It... It's not enough.

17:41.080 --> 17:44.590
She should be fine once the 
bleeding's stopped, right?

17:44.590 --> 17:46.470
That's not enough!

17:46.470 --> 17:48.380
There'll be scars!

17:49.000 --> 17:53.400
The professor loves Madam 
Milk's beautiful fur!

17:53.400 --> 17:55.470
I'm done for...

17:55.860 --> 17:59.500
I'm sorry for making a mess 
of you, too, Madam Milk...

18:00.220 --> 18:01.260
Heal.

18:01.990 --> 18:03.400
What do you think you're doing?!

18:03.400 --> 18:06.100
What's it look like? Casting healing magic.

18:06.100 --> 18:10.750
It's pointless! Maybe you have enough 
magic output to take out a zombie king,

18:10.750 --> 18:13.340
but the kind of finesse needed 
to regenerate skin is...

18:14.480 --> 18:15.860
She's fixed?!

18:15.860 --> 18:18.050
There's no trace of a scar!

18:18.050 --> 18:20.490
Isn't that the kind of magic Heal is?

18:20.490 --> 18:24.240
I fixed the ribs that had been cracked, 
too, so you can continue the walk,

18:24.240 --> 18:27.750
but I'd recommend letting 
her rest for today.

18:29.750 --> 18:32.890
That's not the kind of magic Heal is, man.

18:32.890 --> 18:35.760
Making yourself sound like an elite-grade...

18:37.280 --> 18:42.460
Stop right there, special research student! 
Looking after Madam Milk is my job!

18:50.280 --> 18:52.880
Hello, Zenos... er, Zeno.

18:53.410 --> 18:54.440
What's up?

18:55.750 --> 19:01.110
Well... if you don't mind, 
would you join me for a walk?

19:01.110 --> 19:02.360
A walk?

19:12.440 --> 19:14.710
Is there something you need to tell me?

19:14.710 --> 19:16.990
Well... it's...

19:18.160 --> 19:20.700
I... wanted to apologize.

19:21.760 --> 19:23.190
It's just...

19:24.900 --> 19:26.920
If I were more capable,

19:26.920 --> 19:30.060
I would've been able to get 
Professor Goldran's attention.

19:30.330 --> 19:34.690
Then you wouldn't have 
been dragged into this...

19:34.690 --> 19:37.250
I feel guilty.

19:37.250 --> 19:39.940
And you asked me out for 
a walk to tell me that?

19:39.940 --> 19:45.700
Yes. I'm sure an apology from me 
doesn't amount to much, but...

19:45.700 --> 19:49.300
I'll be taking payment for my efforts 
from Becker, so it's all good.

19:49.300 --> 19:50.710
Don't let it bother you.

19:50.710 --> 19:52.990
Be that as it may...

19:52.990 --> 19:55.210
Besides, without opportunities like these,

19:55.210 --> 19:58.520
I never would've set foot 
inside the Royal Hospital.

19:58.520 --> 20:01.330
I never would've had a chance 
to learn more about my teacher.

20:01.330 --> 20:03.430
There's plenty for me to gain.

20:03.850 --> 20:05.800
So you honestly don't need to worry.

20:06.080 --> 20:10.160
Still, if there's anything 
I can do, just ask.

20:10.810 --> 20:15.280
Come to think of it, what kind 
of person was your teacher?

20:15.280 --> 20:17.950
I honestly don't have much of a clue.

20:17.950 --> 20:22.390
He seemed kinda shady, but he taught me how to 
read and write, and about the outside world,

20:22.390 --> 20:27.080
to say nothing about diseases, injuries, 
and magic. Taught me a whole bunch.

20:27.440 --> 20:29.080
I basically owe him my life.

20:29.080 --> 20:33.460
That sounds a bit like Dr. Becker and myself.

20:33.920 --> 20:35.620
You owe him your life?

20:35.620 --> 20:36.960
Certainly!

20:36.960 --> 20:42.160
When I decided to become a 
healer, he mentored me closely.

20:42.160 --> 20:45.000
Granted, his dedication to research 
caused his girlfriend to leave him,

20:45.000 --> 20:48.680
so I'm basically looking after him...

20:48.680 --> 20:50.270
How do you even know him?

20:50.270 --> 20:51.960
Did I not mention it?

20:51.960 --> 20:54.400
He's my mother's little brother.

20:54.400 --> 20:56.310
My uncle, in other words.

20:56.620 --> 21:00.940
But I didn't amount to much, 
either in magic or in research.

21:00.940 --> 21:03.980
What kind of research are you doing, anyway?

21:03.980 --> 21:07.050
To put it simply, the storage of medication.

21:07.050 --> 21:12.690
At what temperature, what humidity, and 
other factors for how they should be stored.

21:12.690 --> 21:14.320
It's pretty boring.

21:14.320 --> 21:15.420
It is.

21:17.350 --> 21:21.300
But the most important things in 
life tend to be the boring ones.

21:21.300 --> 21:22.540
Zenos...

21:23.050 --> 21:26.300
That's just something my teacher told me.

21:26.300 --> 21:31.810
I was trying to apologize, and 
you ended up cheering me up.

21:31.810 --> 21:35.100
Sometimes it's best to rely on other people.

21:35.100 --> 21:38.120
I get plenty of help in my daily life, too.

21:38.120 --> 21:40.690
I can barely even get out of 
bed on my own in the morning.

21:41.820 --> 21:44.780
You're an interesting person, Zenos.

21:45.630 --> 21:47.440
Another prospective wife, eh?

21:47.440 --> 21:49.070
What was that?

21:49.070 --> 21:51.980
Don't worry about it.
I think we were followed.

21:51.980 --> 21:53.070
By who?

21:53.070 --> 21:57.370
And yet, not as exciting 
as I had hoped. One star.

21:57.370 --> 21:58.840
Quit scoring people.

22:10.180 --> 22:13.060
Please! You've gotta help me!

22:13.340 --> 22:15.310
Uh...

22:15.310 --> 22:16.910
I'm in a real bind here!

22:16.910 --> 22:18.740
Please help me!

22:18.740 --> 22:22.120
Now, this looks interesting! Three stars.

22:22.120 --> 22:24.380
Seriously, no more scores, okay?

23:55.530 --> 24:00.000
A Request from a Noble Lady

23:57.040 --> 23:58.910
"A Request from a Noble Lady."
